Kind: ablation
Issue: #744
Over: 744-widen-no-revoke-notices.patch
Takes out: the block server's own look at a revocation -- a handle no longer asks its token again when the kernel's epoch has moved (004e873f), so with no notice delivered the handle of a revoked capability goes on moving data, as before, and cap_test's [5] reads through it after the revoke
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 1
Expect: cap_test: \[5\] post-revoke read FAIL

diff --git a/uros/src/servers/block_device_server/block_device.c b/uros/src/servers/block_device_server/block_device.c
index 9a7b7038..ddf907be 100644
